# Table Pagination & Search

Every table in this application must paginate. Default **20 per page** with a per-page selector offering **20 / 50 / 100**.

See also: [data-loading.mdc](data-loading.mdc) for async-table mechanics.

## Backend

- Validate `page`, `per_page`, and `search` via `TableDataRequest` (`per_page` allowed: `20,50,100`, default `20`)
- Return paginated JSON via `PaginatedJsonResponse::fromPaginator()` for standard list tables
- Apply `->paginate($request->perPageCount(), ['*'], 'page', $request->pageNumber())` on every `/data` endpoint

## Frontend

- Include a per-page `<select>` with options 20 / 50 / 100 (default selected: 20)
- Pass `getPerPage: () => Number(select?.value ?? 20)` to `initAsyncTable`
- Add a debounced search input (`debounce(..., 300)`) when the table has searchable text columns (name, code, email, etc.)
- Use `renderPagination` from `data-table.js` for page controls

## Non-standard tables

For matrix or card layouts (e.g. inventory color × size grid), paginate the **primary row dimension** and search that dimension. Column headers (sizes) load in full; only rows (colors) paginate.

## Do NOT

- Load entire datasets without pagination
- Use `25` as default or as a per-page option
- Omit search on list tables that display searchable text fields

## Tests

Assert JSON `pagination` shape, default `per_page` of 20, search filtering, and 403 for unauthorized `/data` access.
